# Microstock

- **Activation ≠ entitlement.** The implicit `product_activations` row provisions nothing; usable access is opt-in through a `microstock_workspace_slots` entitlement (`menu_routes = []`, so registry activation never reveals a sidebar node). Slot limit = 1 base when a slot entitlement is active, plus addon quantities, **0** when never activated. `assertCanProvisionMicrostockWorkspace` gates **creation** (422 `workspace_not_activated` / `slot_limit`); resolving an **existing** workspace is never gated. Slot pools are per kind — Microstock never raises `owned_workspace_used`.
- **Never invent credit math client-side.** `AiBillingService::assertCanAnalyze` / `planAnalyze` is the gate; the SPA's Lock & Describe footer pre-flight only blocks when balance < `fileCount × estimate`.
- **Content collaboration is not paid-gated.** A free owner can upload into their collections and an invited member (free or paid) can upload into a shared workspace; `assertCanMutate` is the only upload gate. The paid gate (`assertOwnerEligibleForCollab`) applies to **sharing** (invite/accept) and **creating** workspaces.
- **Public share is blocked** in a system workspace: `VisibilityService::assertSystemWorkspaceShareAllowed` rejects enable (422 `public_share_not_allowed`), and guest `fileAccessible`/`folderAccessible` return false.
- **Billing is prepaid and per HTTP call.** Purchase → `balance_micro_usd`; `planAnalyze` chooses daily-free slots first then prepaid for the remainder; every call writes a `microstock_ai_usage_events` row scoped to `analysis_run_id`; `composeResultFromThinking` settles (debit + `ai_billing` snapshot) **before** promoting `status = generated`. Thinking failure after successful vision triggers a **partial vision settle**. Amounts are **micro-USD** end-to-end and `balance_micro_usd` is **signed** — negative balances are shown, and new paid analyze is blocked until balance ≥ 0.
- **Billing subject** is the user who triggered analyze (`billing_user_id`), not the file uploader — gate, usage events and debit all use that id. Each analyze/re-analyze mints a fresh `analysis_run_id` so re-runs never mix rows.
- **Provider cost is internal.** The customer `BillingUsageEventResource` omits `provider_cost_usd` and the rate snapshot; the admin variant keeps them (response minimization).
- **Daily free** is a Tier B setting: slots reset lazily per calendar day, rows carry `billing_source = daily_free` (no ledger debit, provider cost still recorded), free jobs go to the `*-free` queues and may use separate stage models; an empty free override inherits the paid model. Workers process paid queues first.
- **Collections:** a folder in a Microstock workspace **is** the collection — uploads must live inside one, never the workspace root. `initiate()` rejects (422) a missing `folder_id` or a locked collection; the client mirrors this via `data-workspace-kind` / `data-collection-locked`. State lives on `ARCHIVD_folders` (`collection_status`, `collection_hint` max 2000, `collection_billing_mode`, `collection_locked_at`, `collection_csv_path`); NULL for ordinary Archivd folders. `isCollectionLocked()` covers locked/processing/review/exported.
- **Lifecycle:** `draft` → lock + describe (`POST collections/{folder}/lock`, allowed from draft **and** failed) → `POST …/analyze` (requires locked, non-empty) → `processing` → `review` when **all** assets are terminal → `POST …/export` (requires review) → `exported`. Sub-folders are separate collections and are never processed recursively.
- **Pipeline:** `ProcessCollection` seeds one pending metadata row per file in the folder and dispatches `AnalyzeAssetVision` per file (FIFO by name); each vision persists `ai_vision` and dispatches `AnalyzeAssetThinking`. Dual-lane: vision file N+1 runs while thinking file N runs (default 3+3 per folder, global caps 6 vision / 10 thinking, solo pool 2+2, one thinking job per `metadata_id` via `WithoutOverlapping`). A blocked job is **released**, never failed. Use **Redis** cache in multi-worker deploys so the global counters are cluster-safe.
- **Watchdogs must stay below `DB_QUEUE_RETRY_AFTER` (1800 s)** — `grace_after` and `thinking_grace_after` (600 / 1800) so the watchdog declares failure before the queue re-dispatches a still-running job. `thinking_backlog_after` re-dispatches thinking when vision finished but the thinking job was never queued.
- **Stages are decoupled:** `ai_vision` / `ai_thinking` / `ai_result` each carry status, timestamps, error and output. Thinking failure leaves title/keywords empty with `status = failed` but preserves `ai_vision`. `phase` in API payloads is **derived/presentational — never persisted**; `metadata.status` stays `pending|generated|finalized|failed`.
- **Final curation is manual** (`PATCH assets/{file}/metadata`, `status = finalized`). Export is finalized-only, columns from `microstock.csv.columns`.
- **Prompts:** `Prompts::marketplaceRules()` is the single source injected into **both** stages so they never drift. Titles are natural sentences (40–70 chars, no commas/trademarks/camera specs), keywords are 50–60 terms ordered literal → contextual → conceptual → stylistic (top 10 = literal + contextual only, max 2 stylistic), grounded in **visible content only**. `visionSystem()` / `thinkingSystem()` must stay under ~1200 chars — long system prompts with an image attached return HTTP 524 (unit-tested in `PromptsTest`). Requests pin `temperature = 0.2` + `max_tokens` (2000 single / 4000 batch).
- **Vision delivery defaults to `url`** (signed HTTPS to the persisted `ai_1024` variant); base64 is the fallback and reliably 524s on frontier models. Persisted variants (`ai_512` / `ai_1024`) are what the resolver prefers.
- **Credentials** are envelope-encrypted (`microstock_marketplace_credentials`, resource type `microstock_marketplace_credentials`) — plaintext never reaches the DB; MVP stores/lists/deletes only, no auto-upload. List rows emit query-mode `actions[]` and the SPA maps them into `RowActions`.
- **Operations:** a queue worker (`php artisan microstock:queue-work`) and the scheduler must be running or checksums/analysis silently stall. On Laragon/Windows `queue:work` exits after each job — use the project command.

